688 A dictionary mapping Config modes to a list of associated processing steps.
689 
690 The STEPS dictionary dictates the sequence of functions or operations to be
691 performed based on the selected configuration mode from the Config enumeration.
692 This enables a flexible system where the user can select the desired mode and
693 the system can execute the corresponding steps in sequence.
694 
695 Examples:
696 - For Config.DEFAULT, the system will first generate the code using `simple_gen`,
697   then generate the entry point with `gen_entrypoint`, execute the generated
698   code using `execute_entrypoint`, and finally collect human review using `human_review`.
699 - For Config.LITE, the system will only use the `lite_gen` function to generate the code.
700 
701 This setup allows for modularity and flexibility in handling different user requirements and scenarios.
702 """
